---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Expands the Φ.hone.cap-box marker 114/118 left in a capturing operator's
# state-acc into the boxing call for a PRIMITIVE capture: `Integer.valueOf(I)`,
# `Long.valueOf(J)` or `Double.valueOf(D)`, picked by the marker's type code. The
# shared state is a java/util/List, so a primitive has to become an Object before
# `List.add` can take it; 125 unboxes it again on the way out.
#
# The marker exists so that the peel itself can be ONE rule (see 114's header):
# phino gives each rule its own fixpoint and the plugin runs a single cycle over
# the rule list, so a peel split per capture type could only drain a run whose
# types were already sorted in rule order. This rule carries no such constraint —
# it rewrites the marker where it stands, at any depth and in any order relative to
# its siblings 124/125/126, and its own fixpoint clears every primitive marker in
# the file.
#
# A category-2 (J/D) box takes two stack slots, so its append peaks one slot higher
# than an int's; 112/113 bump the enclosing method's max-stack by 2 whenever the
# factory descriptor carries a J or D, since jeo never recomputes maxs.
name: cap-box-primitive
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-box ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.hone.cap-box, code ↦ 𝑒-code ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-box ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokestatic,
      i2 ↦ 𝑒-owner,
      i3 ↦ "valueOf",
      i4 ↦ 𝑒-descriptor,
      i5 ↦ Φ.false
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
when:
  matches: ['^[IJD]$', 𝑒-code]
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-owner
    function: sed
    args:
      - 𝑒-code
      - '"s/^I$/java\\/lang\\/Integer/"'
      - '"s/^J$/java\\/lang\\/Long/"'
      - '"s/^D$/java\\/lang\\/Double/"'
  - meta: 𝑒-descriptor
    function: sed
    args:
      - 𝑒-code
      - '"s/^I$/(I)Ljava\\/lang\\/Integer;/"'
      - '"s/^J$/(J)Ljava\\/lang\\/Long;/"'
      - '"s/^D$/(D)Ljava\\/lang\\/Double;/"'
